---
/**
 * WikiTip — 첫 화면. (wiki-tip.com)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 저장소 안에 있나 ──────────────────────────────────────
 * Cloudtype 구독 총량 1GB 를 klifemap 과 나눠 쓰는데 여유가 0.25GB 뿐이다.
 * 매체마다 배포를 띄우면 그 자리에서 막힌다. `server.mjs` 가 Host 헤더를 보고
 * wiki-tip.com 요청을 이 경로로 돌린다. **메모리 추가 0원.**
 * (100yearmap.com 과 같은 방식이다)
 *
 * ── 왜 Base 레이아웃을 안 쓰나 ──────────────────────────────────
 * Base 는 SeoulMarkets 의 머리말·꼬리말이 붙어 있다. 그대로 쓰면
 * **금융 매체 얼굴이 K컬처 사이트에 나온다.** 사장님이 Riot 신청 때
 * 「wiki-tip.com 이 케이컬처고 서울마켓츠는 경제/금융이다」라고 지적하신 그 문제다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 광고 금지 ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Riot Production Key 심사 중이다(App 866800). **승인 전에 광고를 달면
 * API 접근이 영구 취소된다.** 이 페이지에는 애드센스 코드를 넣지 않는다.
 * `/esports` 지면도 `Base.astro` 의 `noAds` 로 막아 뒀고 시험으로 증명했다.
 *
 * ── 영문이다 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 사장님 지시: 「모두 영어로 올려야 하는 거 알지? 우리는 영어 사이트야」
 * 1차 독자는 동남아다. 한국어로 쓰면 그 독자에게 안 닿는다.
 */
const TITLE = 'WikiTip — Korean pop culture, explained for Southeast Asia';
const DESC =
  'K-pop, drama, film and esports — reported in English with the numbers behind them. No rumours, no reprints, sources named.';
---

<!-- prettier-ignore -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>{TITLE}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={DESC} />
  <meta property="og:title" content={TITLE} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={DESC} />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <!-- 아직 준비 중이라 색인시키지 않는다. 기사가 채워지면 뗀다. -->
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  <style>
    :root {
      --ink: #1a1626;
      --muted: #635d75;
      --line: #e7e4ee;
      --accent: #6b3fa0;
      --bg: #fcfbfe;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.7;
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
    }
    .wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.25rem 5rem; }
    .logo { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .logo span { color: var(--accent); }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.3; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .lead { font-size: 1.06rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
    .rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 2.5rem 0; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.02rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .beats { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
    .beats li { padding: 0.7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.96rem; }
    .beats b { color: var(--accent); }
    .note { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--muted); }
    .live { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
            color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.1rem 0.6rem; }
    a { color: var(--accent); }
    footer { margin-top: 3.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--muted); }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root { --ink: #ece9f3; --muted: #a49dba; --line: #2b2637; --accent: #b18cf0; --bg: #141119; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="logo">Wiki<span>Tip</span></div>

    <h1>Korean pop culture, with the numbers attached.</h1>
    <p class="lead">{DESC}</p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <h2>Most English coverage of Korean culture is translated gossip.</h2>
    <p>
      A rumour appears in Korean, gets reposted in English a day later, and nobody
      says where it came from. By the time it is corrected, the correction does not travel.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do the opposite. <strong>Every piece starts from something countable</strong> —
      a chart position, a ranked-ladder distribution, a box-office tally, a filing —
      and names where the number came from and when it was measured.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cover</h2>
    <ul class="beats">
      <li><b>K-pop</b> — charts, releases and what the numbers actually show about reach</li>
      <li><b>Drama &amp; film</b> — viewership, box office, and where a title travelled</li>
      <li><b>Esports</b> — Korea's ranked ladder measured against Singapore, Vietnam and Japan <span class="live">live</span></li>
      <li><b>Fandom &amp; industry</b> — how the business behind the culture works</li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <h2>Already running: the ladder census</h2>
    <p>
      Korea is treated as the reference point for competitive play, but almost nobody
      measures how its player base actually differs from its neighbours'.
      We count it daily across six regions and keep the series.
      <strong>A ladder cannot be measured retroactively</strong> — a day not counted is gone.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Built on the Riot Games API. Free to read, no account required.
      <a href="/esports">See the current census →</a>
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <h2>Why Southeast Asia first</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Korean culture travels furthest in Southeast Asia, and the English-language coverage
      written for that audience is thinnest. Singapore and Vietnam are in the esports
      comparison for the same reason — they are the readers, not a footnote.
    </p>

    <footer>
      <p>
        WikiTip is published by the team behind
        <a href="https://seoulmarkets.com">SeoulMarkets</a>, a Korean market data publication.
        Same rule in both places: name the source, state when it was measured,
        and do not publish what has not been verified.
      </p>
      <p class="note">
        This is not investment advice and not affiliated with any agency, label or studio.
        Riot Games does not endorse or sponsor this project.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
